Package: mint-arm-pi
Version: 22.3.6
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Linux Mint ARM local build <mint-arm@localhost>
Depends: linux-image-raspi | linux-image-raspi-realtime, flash-kernel, u-boot-tools, linux-firmware-raspi,
 ubuntu-raspi-settings-desktop
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: Linux Mint ARM64 settings for the Raspberry Pi
 What only the Raspberry Pi uses in the unofficial arm64 build of Linux Mint 22.3, for the
 Raspberry Pi 4, 400 and Compute Module 4 and the Raspberry Pi 5, 500 and Compute Module 5
 (the first start removes this package in a virtual machine).
 It keeps the Pi's boot chain installed: the Raspberry Pi kernel; flash-kernel, which puts
 every new kernel, its initrd and the device trees on the boot partition (using mkimage
 from u-boot-tools); the Pi's boot, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware; and Ubuntu's Raspberry Pi
 desktop settings.
